/-
The block-percolation input of the critical level-set arguments:
Liggett, Schonmann and Stacey, Domination by product measures,
Annals of Probability 25(1), 1997, Corollary 1.4, cited at
sandpile.tex:2589 and sandpile.tex:3992.

The source corollary states that a translation-invariant finite-range
dependent site process on Z^d whose one-site marginals are all at least
1 - delta dominates a Bernoulli site process with parameter p(delta),
where p(delta) -> 1 as delta -> 0.  The paper uses it in dimension two
with p(delta) chosen supercritical, so the dominating Bernoulli process
has an infinite nearest-neighbour component almost surely; that
supercriticality is the standard one-site bound for Bernoulli percolation
on the square lattice.  The combined consequence below is exactly the
form in which the paper applies the corollary: for delta small enough,
every stationary k-dependent planar site process with one-site marginal
at least 1 - delta has an infinite nearest-neighbour component almost
surely.

Stationarity is stated as invariance of the joint law under lattice
shifts.  The dependence range is stated through independence of the
sigma-algebras generated by the site events at Euclidean distance more
than k; since the Euclidean distance dominates the coordinate distance,
this is stronger than the source's block condition at the same range.
The process is indexed by the planar lattice `Sandpile.Site 2` and takes
Boolean values; the open set is the preimage of `true`.
-/
import Sandpile.Support.PercolationEvents
import Sandpile.External.HeatKernelBounds

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Set

-- FROZEN-STATEMENT-BEGIN
/-- Domination of stationary finite-range dependent planar site processes
by supercritical Bernoulli percolation, in the form the paper applies:
for each dependence range, a small enough one-site deficit gives an
infinite component.  Assumed, not proved. -/
def Sandpile.External.LSSDomination : Prop :=
  ∀ k : ℕ,
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧
      ∀ (Ω : Type) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
      [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (X : Sandpile.Site 2 → Ω → Bool),
      (∀ z : Sandpile.Site 2, Measurable (X z)) →
      (∀ w : Sandpile.Site 2,
        MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun ω z => X (z + w) ω) P =
          MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun ω z => X z ω) P) →
      (∀ S T : Set (Sandpile.Site 2), S.Finite → T.Finite →
        (∀ s ∈ S, ∀ t ∈ T, (k : ℝ) < Sandpile.External.latticeDist s t) →
        ProbabilityTheory.Indep
          (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom
            (S.image fun s => {ω : Ω | X s ω = true}))
          (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom
            (T.image fun t => {ω : Ω | X t ω = true})) P) →
      (∀ z : Sandpile.Site 2, 1 - δ ≤ (P {ω : Ω | X z ω = true}).toReal) →
      ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, Sandpile.HasInfiniteComponent {z : Sandpile.Site 2 | X z ω}
-- FROZEN-STATEMENT-END